  "methodological_notes": {
    "note_1": "The study is EXPLANATORY, not FORECASTING. Do not relabel R^2 as predictive.",
    "note_2": "Exogenous variables are contemporaneously aligned, not lagged — deliberate.",
    "note_3": "No shrinkage is applied beyond the numerical stabilizer lambda = 1e-5.",
    "note_4": "The reward is a tuple compared lexicographically; do NOT scalarize.",
    "note_5": "The 3-decimal rounding is load-bearing: it manufactures ties so sparsity and MaxVIF matter.",
    "note_6": "MaxVIF is a TIE-BREAKER, not an additive penalty.",
    "note_7": "Endogenous stopping is implemented entirely as a bias on a_stop.",
    "note_8": "The policy is TABULAR (p x p), not a neural-network function approximator.",
    "note_9": "Eq. (2) is a policy-gradient-style softmax update with one-hot target; no value function, no bootstrapping, no TD error.",
    "note_10": "Ensemble aggregation is linear-coefficient averaging; the average of linear maps is linear (Eq. 12).",
    "note_11": "Iteration budgets were scaled based on empirical convergence during preliminary tuning.",
    "note_12": "Most additional runtime for the endogenous configuration comes from level-1 patience P, not the stopping mechanism.",
    "note_13": "CV-to-test gap is the optimizer's curse, not leakage.",
    "note_14": "The exemplar 15-feature run is a post-hoc best draw; the ensemble average is the headline metric."
  },
